==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{m|sla-pro|*čьto}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{m|ine-pro|*kʷid}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kʷis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-что.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}
* {{IPA|[ʂto]|lang=ru}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|ru|conjunction|head=что|tr=što}} ''(invariable)''

# [[that]]
#:* {{lang|ru|[[я#Russian|Я]] [[думать|ду́маю]], что [[он]] [[дома|до́ма]]}} — ''I think (that) he’s home.''

===Pronoun===
{{head|ru|pronoun|head=что|tr=što}}

# {{context|interrogative|lang=ru}} [[what]]
#:* {{lang|ru|Что [[этот|э́то]]}}? — ''What is this?''
#:* {{lang|ru|[[он|Он]] [[не]] [[знать|знает]], что [[этот|э́то]] [[значить|значит]]}} — ''He doesn’t know what this means.''
# {{context|nonstandard|relative|lang=ru}} [[that]], [[which]]
#:* {{lang|ru|[[книга|кни́га]], что [[на]] [[стол|столе́]]}} — ''the book that is on the table''

====Declension====
{{ru-decl-noun-unc
|[[что́]]
|[[чего|чего́]]
|[[чему|чему́]]
|что́
|[[чем|че́м]]
|о [[чём]]}}
<small>* Letter "{{l|ru|ч}}" in nominative and accusative "что" is pronounced as /ʂ/, not /t͡ɕ/.</small><br>
<small>** Letter "{{l|ru|г}}" in genitive and accusative "чего́" is pronounced as /v/, not /g/.</small>

====Usage notes====
* In informal speech, the genitive form {{l|ru|чего}} often replaces the accusative and sometimes the nominative.

====Synonyms====
* [[чё]] or [[чо]] (čo) (''interrogative pronoun only, non-standard, highly colloquial but common, not used in writing'')
*: Ну чё, пошли́ что ли? — ''Well, let's go!''
*: Чё он хо́чет от меня́? — ''What (the hell) does he want from me?''
* [[шо]] (šo) (''same as above, used in the South of European Russia or by Russian speakers in Ukraine'')
* [[который]] {{qualifier|standard relative pronoun}}

